# Helm CLI conventions

This is an ESM-only React + Ink terminal app. When editing `src/`:

- **Always use explicit `.js` extensions in relative imports** (e.g.
  `import { db } from '../db/client.js'`), even for `.ts`/`.tsx` files. This is
  required by the `Bundler` module resolution + ESM output.
- **Never add `import React from 'react'`.** The automatic JSX runtime is on and
  `noUnusedLocals` will fail the build. Import only hooks you actually use
  (`import { useState } from 'react'`). Use the `React.` namespace only in files
  that already import it for types.
- **Keep `src/core/**` free of React/Ink.** Domain logic (db, prompts, todos,
  util) must stay UI-agnostic so it is testable in isolation.
- **Use design tokens from `src/theme/theme.ts`** (colors, gradients, symbols,
  priorityMeta). Do not hardcode hex colors inside components/screens.
- **Add new screens** under `src/screens/<feature>/`, register them in
  `src/app.tsx`, and add the route to the union in
  `src/navigation/routes.ts`.
- **Data layout is git-ignored:** prompts as `prompts/<project>/<slug>.md`,
  SQLite at `data/helm.db`. Resolve paths via `src/config/paths.ts` only — never
  hardcode these locations. Never commit the `prompts/` or `data/` folders.
- **SQLite storage:** dates as ISO-8601 strings, booleans as `0/1` integers.
  Schema changes go in `src/core/db/schema.ts` + `src/core/db/migrate.ts`.
- Run `pnpm types:check` after changes; the build must stay clean.
- Follow `quality-gates.mdc`: update tests in `__tests__/`, keep `/docs` in sync, pass format/lint/types/tests.
